<title>HUNGARY: Hungarian parties want NATO referendum by November.</title>
<headline>Hungarian parties want NATO referendum by November.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's seven parliamentary parties agreed on Thursday that a referendum on NATO membership should be called by the end of November, the Hungarian news agency MTI said.</p>
<p>The parties also agreed parliament will on July 15 formally approve a statement in appreciation of Tuesday's decision at the Madrid NATO summit to invite Hungary, Poland and the Czech Republic for membership talks.</p>
<p>All parties have welcomed NATO's gesture and said the decision recognised efforts by the three Central European states to integrate with the West.</p>
</text>
